-- check/bad (core): a `foreign type` has no body to derive an ordering
-- over, so it answers `<` only through §3.2's table or through a `pub
-- compare` of its own module (A.50) — and a type that WRAPS one inherits
-- exactly that (A.54).
--
-- `Wraps` was accepted and derived a `compare` whose one part was `err`:
-- `equatable` is the only transitive gate the checker had, and it says
-- nothing about ordering. `compare` now has a `comparable` twin settled by
-- the same fixpoint.
--
-- `Hidden` is the control, and the second half of A.55: `Key` IS equatable,
-- so `==` on a `Hidden` resolves — but through `Basics.eq`, the one
-- structural walk, and NOT by minting a derived row for a foreign type S5
-- has no body to emit.
pub foreign type Handle


pub equatable foreign type Key


pub type Wraps
    = Wraps Handle


pub opaque type Hidden
    = Hidden Key


pub before : Wraps, Wraps -> Bool
before a b =
    a < b
